{"name":"Bugle Boy","hex":"#bb8f4f","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bugle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A horn used by hunters.","A simple brass instrument consisting of a horn with no valves, playing only pitches in its harmonic series"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To announce, sing, or cry in the manner of a musical bugle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bugle"},{"term":"boy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Bodo (Central Africa)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A male child. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A young man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bugle Boy","blocks":[{"text":"Bugle Boy Industries, Inc. was an American apparel company best known for its jeans and casual pants—including parachute pants and cargo pants—and for its television advertising during the 1980s and 1990s. The company was founded in 1977 by engineer and entrepreneur William C. W. Mow as Buckaroo International, Inc., and was renamed Bugle Boy Industries in 1980. The company was privately held and grew into one of the largest apparel firms in Southern California, with annual sales of roughly $500 million, before filing for Chapter 11 bankruptcy and being liquidated in 2001. Its trademark and wholesale operations were sold to Schottenstein Stores Corp. for $68.6 million."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bugle_Boy"},{"title":"Bugle","blocks":[{"text":"The bugle is a simple signaling brass instrument with a wide conical bore. It normally has no valves or other pitch-altering devices, and is thus limited to its natural harmonic notes, and pitch is controlled entirely by varying the air and embouchure."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Bugle_in_C_MET_DP-12679-123.jpg/330px-Bugle_in_C_MET_DP-12679-123.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bugle"},{"title":"Boy","blocks":[{"text":"A boy is a young male human. The term is commonly used for a child or an adolescent. When a male human reaches adulthood, they are usually described as a man."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg/330px-Smiling_little_boy_of_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Museo_Numantino_-_Trompa.jpg/120px-Museo_Numantino_-_Trompa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Museo_Numantino_-_Trompa.jpg/250px-Museo_Numantino_-_Trompa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Museo_Numantino_-_Trompa.jpg/120px-Museo_Numantino_-_Trompa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseo_Numantino_-_Trompa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/1911_EB_Roman_Bugle.png/120px-1911_EB_Roman_Bugle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/1911_EB_Roman_Bugle.png/250px-1911_EB_Roman_Bugle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/1911_EB_Roman_Bugle.png/120px-1911_EB_Roman_Bugle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1911_EB_Roman_Bugle.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Pilaster_of_Angels_Sounding_Trumpets_from_the_Parapet_of_a_Pulpit_MET_DP169508.jpg/120px-Pilaster_of_Angels_S